# third_party/VENDOR.ndb: one record per vendored import (docs/04 §3.1, ADR-0003).
# Each tree under third_party/ is the upstream release, unchanged. sha256= is the
# release tarball; for an import from a source tree that has no release,
# git.tree= is instead the directory's git tree id at the commit upstream= pins
# (git write-tree over the files reproduces it). tree.sha256= is the unpacked
# tree, as this prints inside it:
#   find . -type f -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
# `./build vendor-check` recomputes it.
# subset= lists the parts of a larger release that were kept, paths as in the
# release; tree.sha256= is then over just those.

